Subject: [PATCH 24/40] Multithreaded engine: OPENEMS_FUSED_STAT, the time
 split of the fused sweep per thread

OPENEMS_FUSED_STAT=1 times every thread of the fused sweep: its sweep, the wait at the first barrier, the
currents of the line before its slab and the wait at the second barrier, summed since the slabs were set up
and printed when the thread count changes or the engine is reset. A diagnostic only (the timing is one
branch on a static flag per timestep when it is off); it showed where 8 threads lose time on the Apple M5
(at 8 threads the threads waited 24-27 % of every timestep at the barriers on the patch x5, notch x3, SMA
and GCPW models, under about 1.4 cores of other load), which the neighbour flags of a later commit address.

Generated-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
Signed-off-by: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
